      "narrative": "Kael, you lean across the scarred table toward Mara Venn. Her sharp eyes flick up from the rim of her cup as you ask about the Ash Gate \u2014 why it's sealed, what she knows.\n\nShe sets the cup down. A pause. Her fingers drum once on the wood.\n\n\"The Ash Gate,\" she says slowly, \"has been closed since the night Old Bram died. That much is common knowledge. The lockwright, Toran Vex \u2014\" she nods toward the nervous clerk at the bar, \"\u2014 he's the one who set the seal. Swears he did it by the Kestrel Guild's book.\"\n\nShe stops. Her jaw tightens. She's holding something back \u2014 you can feel it in the beat of silence, the way her gaze drifts past you to the shuttered windows. There's a detail she's decided not to share, some thread she's weighing whether to pull.\n\n\"Beyond that?\" She shrugs, a little too casually. \"I'm just a woman with questions, not answers. You'd have to ask the Guild what they think lies on the other side.\"\n\nBut you notice: she didn't say she doesn't know. She said she won't say."
    },
