      "narrative": "You ask the question, but something's off. The words come out wrong \u2014 tangled, rushed. You meant \"filed\" as in *sealed*, but it lands sideways. Mara Venn's brow furrows.\n\n\"Filed?\" she repeats, the word strange in her mouth. She tilts her head, studying you like you've just spoken in a language she half-recognizes. \"You mean the seal. The lock.\"\n\nShe waits for you to correct yourself, but the moment stretches thin. Toran Vex glances over from the bar, ink-stained fingers frozen mid-wrap around his cup. He heard the stumble.\n\nMara exhales slowly, disappointment flickering behind her eyes. She picks up her cup, takes a long drink, and sets it down with a deliberate *clink*.\n\n\"Toran Vex,\" she says flatly, \"is the lockwright. He maintained the gate's lock for years. Sworn to the Kestrel Guild. He set the seal the night Bram died. That's what I know.\"\n\nShe doesn't elaborate. The question you asked \u2014 the one you *meant* to ask \u2014 has passed. She answered what you said, not what you intended, and she's not inclined to bridge the gap.\n\nThe tavern creaks. A log settles in the hearth. The silence between you curdles into something uncomfortable.\n\nMara looks at you sidelong. \"Was that all? Or was there something else you wanted to ask?\""
    },
